{
  "name": "iso27001",
  "annotations": [
    {
      "tag": "standard",
      "value": "ISO/IEC 27001:2022"
    },
    {
      "tag": "edition",
      "value": "3"
    },
    {
      "tag": "publication_date",
      "value": "2022-10-25"
    },
    {
      "tag": "amendment",
      "value": "ISO/IEC 27001:2022/Amd 1:2024"
    },
    {
      "tag": "amendment_publication_date",
      "value": "2024-02-23"
    },
    {
      "tag": "overview_and_terms",
      "value": "ISO/IEC 27000:2026"
    },
    {
      "tag": "iso_open_data_date",
      "value": "2026-10-28"
    }
  ],
  "description": "A LinkML model of the records an organization keeps to run an information security management system (ISMS) to ISO/IEC 27001:2022 with Amendment 1:2024: its context and scope, policies, roles and objectives, risks and their treatment, its controls and Statement of Applicability, the support and operation it needs, its audits and management reviews, and its nonconformities, corrective actions and improvements. The 93 reference controls of Annex A appear by their numbers alone.",
  "title": "ISO/IEC 27001:2022 information security management system records",
  "comments": [
    "The version is the edition the schema models, 2022, with its one amendment, Amd 1:2024, and source is ISO's page for that edition. ISO Open Data's records of both, and of ISO/IEC 27002:2022 and ISO/IEC 27000:2026, are copied to src/iso27001/schema/iso-open-data/ as of the date in the annotations, and scripts/check_upstream_release.py reports when ISO publishes another supplement or edition. The release tags are the schema's own versions.",
    "ISO/IEC 27001 is copyright ISO and IEC, and none of its text is reproduced here. Each element cites the clause or Annex A control it models by number, in the iso27001_clause or annex_a_control annotation, and its description is this project's own words. A licence holder can merge the standard's wording into a private copy with the overlay that src/iso27001/schema/OVERLAY.md describes.",
    "The terms follow ISO/IEC 27000, which ISO/IEC 27001 refers to for them; the edition current on the pinned date is ISO/IEC 27000:2026.",
    "Every record that other records refer to has an isms_id, and a reference holds that identifier. IsmsManagementSystem holds each kind of record in a list of its own.",
    "The mappings name terms of the released lmodel/oscal, lmodel/spdx and lmodel/nist-sp-800-53 schemas, and come from the SSSOM files in src/iso27001/mappings/."
  ],
  "source": "https://www.iso.org/standard/82875.html",
  "see_also": [
    "https://lmodel.github.io/iso27001",
    "https://www.iso.org/standard/82875.html",
    "https://www.iso.org/standard/88435.html"
  ],
  "id": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso27001",
  "version": "2022/Amd 1:2024",
  "imports": [
    "linkml:types"
  ],
  "license": "Apache-2.0",
  "prefixes": [
    {
      "prefix_prefix": "linkml",
      "prefix_reference": "https://w3id.org/linkml/"
    },
    {
      "prefix_prefix": "iso27001",
      "prefix_reference": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso27001/"
